{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"Criar monitoramento"},"description":"Creates a signal monitor. Default: a MARKET monitor, with no source sheet: { mode: 'market', name, market: { category, ...filters }, dailyLimit }. Every day (or week) it searches the signal over that market and saves only companies it has not delivered yet into a companies sheet, created with the monitor's name unless destinationSheetId is given. Market categories: hiring needs hiringTitle, and industry keeps it to the ICP's sector in plain words; funding needs periodDays 7/30/90/180 and cnpj periodDays 7/30/90 (cnpj.event picks the registry event, opening by default); news needs categories and periodDays; location narrows it; tech is online stores by what their sites run (market.stores with platforms, crms, withoutCrms, noCrm, trafficTiers, states, city, companySizes, withDecisionMaker; only on workspaces that have the store search); custom is a very specific ask checked company by company (market { category: 'custom', source, rules }, the same source and rules format as the rules-based company search; every company is checked once; 2 credits per company checked plus 2 per company that passed); job_change is people new in a role, delivered into a people sheet (market { category: 'job_change', jobTitle, periodDays 30/60/90, location, industry, companySizes, domains, move }; 4 credits per person, no contact); construction is companies that registered a construction project at the Receita's CNO, \"Iniciou uma constru\u00e7\u00e3o\" (market { category: 'construction', periodDays 7/30/90, location with a state, minAreaM2 optional }; 2 credits per company; cite Receita Federal (CNO)); growth is companies whose team grew (market { category: 'growth', minGrowthPct, months 6 or 12, location, industry, companySizes }; 2 credits per company); ads is companies running ads (market { category: 'ads', query } for a theme on Meta, or { category: 'ads', domains } for up to 10 accounts on Google; with start \"future\" only the ones that start advertising arrive; 4 credits per company); erp is companies that run a given ERP, proved with public evidence (a job post, the site or the domain's e-mail; call it \"Usa ERP\"): market { category: 'erp', erps (any of totvs, sap_business_one, sap, omie, sankhya, senior, linx, netsuite, dynamics, bling, tiny, contaazul, egestor, vhsys, marketup, gestaoclick, nomus; sap_business_one needs evidence naming Business One), hiringArea (the openings that bring the candidates, default fiscal_contabil; also fiscal, contabil, controladoria, financeiro, compras), location, industry, companySizes }; 4 credits per company delivered (8 when a job post read from the job index proved it), plus 4 per job post read and 1 per other company checked, proved or not; there is no one-off ERP search, only this monitor; site_tech is companies by what their site loads (market { category: 'site_tech', technologies, change uses/adopted/removed, domains or location/industry/companySizes }; 2 credits per company, and in a market each company checked costs the same; adopted and removed deliver from the second run on); email_engagement, followers and competitor_intent are free people monitors (market { category, ...filters }, delivered into a people sheet, no contact); followers needs start \"future\" to deliver only new ones; competitor_intent with emailDigest true and frequency weekly e-mails the user who rose to the top; reviews and trade_show are company monitors, and with start \"future\" they deliver only new reviews or new exhibitors; visitor is the companies the workspace's own website tracker identified (it requires the tracker installed): market { category: 'visitor', periodDays 7/14/30, minStrength 0-100, buyingPagesOnly }, 2 credits per company plus the contact as usual; the visit only times the message and is not cited in it. contact: { jobTitle, withEmail } also finds one person with that title at each company (hiring, funding, news, growth, ads, erp and custom; jobTitles adds titles tried in order, location narrows the person, excludeTitles leaves titles out) and, with withEmail, their work e-mail: +2 credits per person found, +3 per e-mail found. Charged per company delivered (4 credits; 2 for cnpj; a store 6, +2 with its owner, +3 with a contact e-mail), at most dailyLimit (default 10, up to 25) a day; a search with nothing new is free. start: { past: N } makes the first run bring up to N companies the market already has (charged as usual), \"future\" brings only what appears from now on; without it the first run brings up to dailyLimit. List form, to follow the companies of an existing sheet: category plus sheetId and that signal's fields (hiring, news, funding, tech, cnpj, crm, job_change; social watches a topic), spending up to the monthly credit limit set. A cnpj list with events (branch, mei_exit, simples_exit, new_partner, gov_contract, debt_new, capital_up, address_change, cnae_change) follows those Registry events of the sheet's companies (a portfolio of CNPJs), free; without events it checks openings, charged per CNPJ. A social topic signal (category social, mode \"topic\", query, sources, maxItems) finds every day who posts about the topic: sources linkedin and reddit, plus x, instagram and tiktok for creators, small businesses and consumers (those three cost 2 credits per person found; instagram reads the words as a hashtag or keyword, so short words work best). An engagement signal (category social, mode \"engagement\", watch \"own\", \"competitors\" with competitors by name, or \"people\" with people: up to 10 LinkedIn profile URLs or { linkedinUrl, name, company }; jobTitle, maxItems, monthlyCreditLimit) finds every day who reacted to or commented on the user's own posts (the company page, the founders and the connected LinkedIn accounts), the competitors' posts (pages and founders; people adds profiles), or the named people's posts (e.g. a competitor's CEO); it does not include their colleagues; 12 credits per new person. activate: true runs it once right away; a market monitor's run goes on in the background (finding people takes minutes), so its first companies land in its sheet shortly after and the immediate result carries no final count.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","properties":{"monitor":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"activate":{"type":"boolean"},"contact":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"excludeTitles":{"items":{"maxLength":200,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"maxItems":20,"type":"array"},"groups":{"items":{"enum":["owners","sales","marketing","ecommerce","technology","finance","people","operations"],"type":"string"},"maxItems":3,"type":"array"},"jobTitle":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"jobTitles":{"items":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"maxItems":10,"type":"array"},"location":{"maxLength":200,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"withEmail":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["jobTitle"],"type":"object"},"dailyLimit":{"maximum":25,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"destinationSheetId":{"format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$","type":"string"},"frequency":{"enum":["daily","weekly"],"type":"string"},"market":{"oneOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"category":{"const":"tech","type":"string"},"stores":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"city":{"maxLength":80,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"companySizes":{"items":{"enum":["ME","EPP","DEMAIS"],"type":"string"},"maxItems":3,"type":"array"},"crms":{"items":{"enum":["rdstation","edrone","klaviyo","martz","dito"],"type":"string"},"maxItems":5,"type":"array"},"noCrm":{"type":"boolean"},"platforms":{"items":{"enum":["nuvemshop"